{"id":"twitter:1845824868526239891","tweet_id":"1845824868526239891","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1845824868526239891","title":"@snaggle_fang @NBCNews I am asking an academic question from a purely methodoligcal point of view Usually after labor day you start to see most pollst","summary":"@snaggle_fang @NBCNews I am asking an academic question from a purely methodoligcal point of view Usually after labor day you start to see most pollsters moving to likely versus registered voters. This cycle I am seeing both methods and then mixing these polls in averages Just curious","date":"2024-10-14","published":"2024-10-14T13:51:57+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/i/status/1845823852284129400","reply_tweet_id":"1845823852284129400","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@snaggle_fang @NBCNews I am asking an academic question from a purely methodoligcal point of view<br><br>Usually after labor day you start to see most pollsters moving to likely versus registered voters.<br><br>This cycle I am seeing both methods and then mixing these polls in averages<br><br>Just curious</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1845824868526239891","display_date":"October 14, 2024 · 13:51 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
