{"id":"twitter:2044411433253741031","tweet_id":"2044411433253741031","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2044411433253741031","title":"I wonder how the Supreme Court would come down on this. States are allowed to allocate their Electoral College votes however they please. So the Popul","summary":"I wonder how the Supreme Court would come down on this. States are allowed to allocate their Electoral College votes however they please. So the Popular Vote Pact doesn't usurp Federal power. That has been the legal standard used for the Compact Clause https://x.com/EricaRN4USA/status/2044198014793797927","date":"2026-04-15","published":"2026-04-15T13:44:03+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>I wonder how the Supreme Court would come down on this.<br><br>States are allowed to allocate their Electoral College votes however they please.<br><br>So the Popular Vote Pact doesn&#x27;t usurp Federal power.<br><br>That has been the legal standard used for the Compact Clause <a href=\"https://x.com/EricaRN4USA/status/2044198014793797927\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://x.com/EricaRN4USA/status/2044198014793797927</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2044411433253741031","display_date":"April 15, 2026 · 13:44 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
